{"name":"Green Goth Eyeshadow","hex":"#588266","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"goth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A punk-derived subculture of people who predominantly dress in black and usually old fashioned clothing, associated with mournful and macabre music and attitudes.","A style of punk rock influenced by glam rock; gothic rock."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to goth music or people."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goth"},{"term":"eyeshadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of eye shadow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyeshadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eye shadow","blocks":[{"text":"Eye shadow is a cosmetic applied primarily to the eyelids to attract attention to the wearer's eyes, making them stand out or look more attractive. Eye shadow can also be applied under the eyes, on the cheeks, or to brow bones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Colours_-_make_up.jpg/330px-Colours_-_make_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_shadow","wikidata":"Q964307"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Duochrome_super_macro_eye_shadow_by_m.a.c.%2C_ben_nye%2C_and_coastal_scents..jpg/500px-Duochrome_super_macro_eye_shadow_by_m.a.c.%2C_ben_nye%2C_and_coastal_scents..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Duochrome_super_macro_eye_shadow_by_m.a.c.%2C_ben_nye%2C_and_coastal_scents..jpg/500px-Duochrome_super_macro_eye_shadow_by_m.a.c.%2C_ben_nye%2C_and_coastal_scents..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A mainly purple eye shadow look, with a brown shade blended in on the top.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADuochrome_super_macro_eye_shadow_by_m.a.c.%2C_ben_nye%2C_and_coastal_scents..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/A_woman_wearing_Eye_Shadow.jpg/500px-A_woman_wearing_Eye_Shadow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/A_woman_wearing_Eye_Shadow.jpg/1280px-A_woman_wearing_Eye_Shadow.jpg